; ted-fileopen2-outmem-freed (#1009): fileopen2 frees the old text
; (freeall) and then allocates the first line of the new one; when that
; fails, outmem redraws from the freed lines and the editor goes on with
; them.  TED alone under inject (alerts answered, track: the allocations
; left when TED ends), a text of one line (a line item of 46 bytes); Open
; of a file whose first line makes a line item of 50 bytes, whose
; AllocMem fails.  Then "q" typed, SAVE under a new name, QUIT.
; Correct (the fix of the issue): the alert "Not enough memory for
; operation!", the old text freed, an empty text to go on with ("q" is
; saved), nothing left allocated.
; @fixed #1009
; @file bo.bas "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789\n"
; @file other.bas "0123456789012345678901234567890123456789\n"
; @source F bo.bas
; @command TEDAB:tools/inject alerts track allocfail=50-50/f=1/1 blitz2:ted @FILE@
; @expect stdout "inject: allocfail: 1 allocations failed"
; @expect stdout "inject: alert: Not enough memory for operation!"
; @expect nostdout "inject:   46 bytes, flags $1\n"
; @expect data new.bas "q\n"
timeout 20
wait screen
menu 0 1
wait freq "Name of file to load"
freq ok "TEDRUN:work/other.bas"
wait screen
type "q"
menu 0 2
wait freq "Name to save file as"
freq ok "TEDRUN:work/new.bas"
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
